#: ../../source/docs/common-scripted-aerobatics-4.4.rst:225
#: 9b51ef1e4eda4668b5284becb8478078
msgid "Other scripts can be developed which allow control of the vehicle, either via NAV_SCRIPT_TIME mission items or from normal flight modes. The key calls are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripted-aerobatics-4.4.rst:227
#: b24e43f3c86a4aaea669859ec356ad9c
msgid "Enabling scripting control override of roll/pitch/yaw rates and throttle with a specific call \"vehicle:nav_scripting_enable(..)\" which returns a boolean indicating  success or failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripted-aerobatics-4.4.rst:229
#: 192dca6a116e4346a7ccf6838811136d
msgid "Obtaining the arguments of a NAV_SCRIPT_TIME command using \"vehicle:nav_script_time()\" if running while in AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripted-aerobatics-4.4.rst:231
#: 1c858872e3994440ab14d3b36fba73ed
msgid "Controlling the above rates and throttle with the \"vehicle:set_target_throttle_rate_rpy(....)\" function, which must be called regularly (at least every second) to set the roll/pitch/yaw rates and throttle percentage. Failure to do so, will disable the control override and return control to the original flight mode. Changing flight modes also disables script control."
msgstr ""
